        "title": "Hull Form and Resistance",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The water resists every metre a ship moves. That resistance — and the engine power\nneeded to overcome it — is the single biggest driver of fuel cost, emissions, and the\nchoice of hull shape. The crucial discovery, due to William Froude in the 1860s-70s,\nis that ship resistance is not one thing but a *sum of separable components* that obey\n*different scaling laws*. Splitting them is what lets us test a 5-metre model in a tank\nand confidently predict the drag of a 300-metre ship."
    },
