        "title": "Hull Form and Resistance",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The whole guide hangs off this one diagram. Frictional resistance scales by Reynolds\nnumber; wave-making by Froude number; they cannot be matched simultaneously in a model,\nso Froude *separated* them. (For the general physics of skin friction and wave drag, see\n`fluid-dynamics/04-BOUNDARY-LAYERS.md` and `fluid-dynamics/08-HYDRODYNAMICS.md`; this\nguide specializes that physics to the hull-and-free-surface problem.)"
    },
